---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="pace: company-wide skills for AI coding agents"
  description="One router, many commands across engineering, product, ops, and marketing. For design, pace defers to impeccable."
  activeNav="home"
  canonicalPath="/"
>
  <!-- ============================================
       HERO
       ============================================ -->
  <section class="hero" id="hero">
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <div class="hero-left">
        <h1 class="hero-title">pace</h1>
        <p class="hero-tagline">Company-wide skills for AI coding agents.</p>

        <p class="hero-lede">
          A curated Claude Code marketplace plus a company router. Install the <code>/pace</code> router for GoldenBerry-specific commands, plus any of <strong>49 plugins</strong> from <a href="https://github.com/anthropics/knowledge-work-plugins" class="hero-link">Anthropic's knowledge-work-plugins</a> and partners: sales, marketing, finance, legal, engineering, data, customer support, product, HR, ops, design, and more. For frontend code design, pace defers to <a href="https://impeccable.style" class="hero-link">impeccable</a>.
        </p>

        <div class="hero-included">
          <span class="hero-included-label">What's included</span>
          <div class="hero-included-row">
            <span><em>/pace</em> company router</span>
            <span class="hero-sep">·</span>
            <span>17 first-party + 5 partner-built plugins</span>
            <span class="hero-sep">·</span>
            <span>27 external plugins by reference</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hero-cta-row">
          <a href="#downloads" class="cta cta-primary">Get started</a>
          <a href="/plugins" class="cta cta-secondary">Browse the catalog</a>
        </div>

        <div class="hero-harnesses">
          <span class="hero-harnesses-label">Works with</span>
          <ul class="hero-harnesses-list">
            <li>Cursor</li>
            <li>Claude Code</li>
            <li>Gemini CLI</li>
            <li>Codex CLI</li>
            <li>VS Code Copilot</li>
            <li>Kiro</li>
            <li>OpenCode</li>
            <li>Pi</li>
            <li>Qoder</li>
            <li>RovoDev</li>
            <li>Trae</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="hero-right" aria-label="Quick install">
        <div class="hero-terminal">
          <div class="terminal-bar">
            <span class="terminal-dot" data-dot="r"></span>
            <span class="terminal-dot" data-dot="y"></span>
            <span class="terminal-dot" data-dot="g"></span>
            <span class="terminal-label">install pace</span>
          </div>
          <pre class="terminal-body"><code><span class="prompt">$</span> claude plugin marketplace add \
    GoldenBerry-SO/pace.tools
<span class="muted">Registers 50 plugins.</span>
<span class="prompt">$</span> claude plugin install sales@pace.tools
<span class="prompt">$</span> /sales:call-prep Acme Corp</code></pre>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================================
       01. THE FOUNDATION
       ============================================ -->
  <section class="section foundation" id="foundation">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="section-number">01</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">The Foundation</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="section-body">
      <p class="section-lede">
        Pace is two things in one repo: a Claude Code marketplace that registers <strong>50 plugins</strong>, and a GoldenBerry-specific <code>/pace</code> router for our internal way of working. Both halves install independently and coexist.
      </p>

      <div class="foundation-grid">
        <article class="foundation-card">
          <h3>The marketplace manifest</h3>
          <p><code>.claude-plugin/marketplace.json</code> registers every plugin in this repo plus external git references. Adding the marketplace once gives Claude visibility to all 50.</p>
          <span class="foundation-card-status">One source of truth</span>
        </article>
        <article class="foundation-card">
          <h3>Plugins as folders</h3>
          <p>Each plugin lives at <code>plugins/&lt;name&gt;/</code> with its own <code>plugin.json</code>, <code>skills/</code> directory, and optional <code>.mcp.json</code> for connectors. Self-contained; we don't edit them.</p>
          <span class="foundation-card-status">Verbatim from upstream</span>
        </article>
        <article class="foundation-card">
          <h3>The /pace router</h3>
          <p>One skill at <code>skill/</code> for company-specific commands. Reads <code>PRODUCT.md</code> for context. Sub-commands ship as we author them, layered on top of the marketplace.</p>
          <span class="foundation-card-status">GoldenBerry-authored</span>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="foundation-cta">
        <p>
          Register the marketplace once with <code><span class="slash">$</span> claude plugin marketplace add GoldenBerry-SO/pace.tools</code>, then install only the plugins your team needs.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================================
       02. THE LANGUAGE
       ============================================ -->
  <section class="section language" id="language">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="section-number">02</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">The Catalog</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="section-body">
      <p class="section-lede">
        Pace is a marketplace. Install the <code>/pace</code> router for GoldenBerry-specific commands, and pick the department plugins your team actually needs. Built on the verbatim import of <a href="https://github.com/anthropics/knowledge-work-plugins">Anthropic's knowledge-work-plugins</a>.
      </p>

      <div class="catalog-grid">
        <article class="catalog-card catalog-card-router">
          <div class="catalog-card-meta">
            <span class="catalog-card-prefix">/pace</span>
            <span class="catalog-card-tag">Router</span>
          </div>
          <h3>Company router</h3>
          <p>GoldenBerry-specific commands. Empty in v0.1; we add as we author. <code>/pace teach</code> sets up project context.</p>
          <span class="catalog-card-author">GoldenBerry</span>
        </article>

        <article class="catalog-card">
          <div class="catalog-card-meta">
            <span class="catalog-card-prefix">/sales:*</span>
            <span class="catalog-card-tag">9 workflows</span>
          </div>
          <h3>Sales</h3>
          <p>Prospect, prep calls, manage pipeline, draft outreach, build battlecards.</p>
          <span class="catalog-card-author">Anthropic</span>
        </article>

        <article class="catalog-card">
          <div class="catalog-card-meta">
            <span class="catalog-card-prefix">/marketing:*</span>
            <span class="catalog-card-tag">8 workflows</span>
          </div>
          <h3>Marketing</h3>
          <p>Draft content, plan campaigns, enforce brand voice, brief on competitors, report performance.</p>
          <span class="catalog-card-author">Anthropic</span>
        </article>

        <article class="catalog-card">
          <div class="catalog-card-meta">
            <span class="catalog-card-prefix">/engineering:*</span>
            <span class="catalog-card-tag">10 workflows</span>
          </div>
          <h3>Engineering</h3>
          <p>Standups, code review, architecture decisions, incident response, tech docs.</p>
          <span class="catalog-card-author">Anthropic</span>
        </article>

        <article class="catalog-card">
          <div class="catalog-card-meta">
            <span class="catalog-card-prefix">/data:*</span>
            <span class="catalog-card-tag">10 workflows</span>
          </div>
          <h3>Data</h3>
          <p>Write SQL, visualize, validate analyses, ship dashboards. Snowflake, Databricks, BigQuery.</p>
          <span class="catalog-card-author">Anthropic</span>
        </article>

        <article class="catalog-card">
          <div class="catalog-card-meta">
            <span class="catalog-card-prefix">/finance:*</span>
            <span class="catalog-card-tag">8 workflows</span>
          </div>
          <h3>Finance</h3>
          <p>Journal entries, reconciliation, statements, variance analysis, close support.</p>
          <span class="catalog-card-author">Anthropic</span>
        </article>

        <article class="catalog-card">
